### Quick tips for a Norway road‑trip in late November

| Tip | Why it matters |
|-----|-----------------|
| **Winter tyres** (mandatory from 1 Dec) | All rental cars are delivered with winter tyres; double‑check the tyre label before you drive. |
| **Snow‑chains** | Required on some mountain passes when conditions are severe; they are already included in the winterisation fee. |
| **Daylight** | Expect ~5–6 hours of daylight in southern Norway in early December – plan scenic stops (e.g., Lillehammer, Geiranger, Hardanger) accordingly. |
| **Fuel** | Most stations accept credit‑card pre‑authorisation; keep the tank at least half full when you return the car to avoid extra charges. |
| **Road‑tolls & ferries** | Many routes have electronic tolls (AutoPASS). The rental contract usually includes a toll‑pass; confirm with Alamo. |

